The presence of differences in how the statements are evaluated across different batches is evident from the previous analyses. To investigate whether the same statements are consistently ranked across batches, the \index{$\uprho$}$\uprho$, \index{$\uptau$}$\uptau$, and rank-biased overlap (\index{RBO}RBO) \cite{webber2010similarity} correlation coefficients are computed. These are calculated between the scores aggregated using the mean across batches, within each \politifact category. The RBO parameter is configured so that the top-5 results receive approximately 85\% of the evaluation weight.

