\section{Experimental Setup}
\vspace*{-0.2cm}
\subsection{Model Specifications}
\label{subsec:model}
video-SALMONN 2 is built on an internally trained high-performance visual LLM, which is further fine-tuned on LLaVA-OneVision-7B \cite{li2024llavaov}. The model processes video frames at a per-second frame rate of 1 (\textit{i.e.}, $\phi=1$), and can handle up to 110 frames. For videos longer than 110 seconds, 110 frames are uniformly sampled from the video.

For the audio branch, we use the Whisper-Large-v3 encoder \cite{radford2023robust} as the audio encoder, and a window-level Q-Former \cite{tang2024extending} with a window length of 0.5 seconds as the audio aligner, producing a total of 60 audio tokens for a 30-second input. The Whisper encoder has a maximum processing duration of $t_{\text{max}} = 30$ seconds.
The rank $r$ and scaling factor $\alpha$ of LoRA are set to 128 and 2.0, respectively. During training, the visual encoder, the audio encoder, and LLM remain frozen.

