\subsubsection{Sensitivity to \Frac{} times.}
Fig.~\ref{fig:04-Evaluation2} compares the performance sensitivity of \MAJ{5} to the number of \Frac{} operations.
PUDTune consistently outperforms the baseline with lower ECR and higher throughput across all configurations.
The $\text{T}_{2,1,0}$ configuration delivers optimal results, achieving \majxThroughputGrainSpeedup{}$\times$ improvement over $\text{T}_{0,0,0}$ and \majxThroughputWideSpeedup{}$\times$ over $\text{T}_{2,2,2}$.
These results confirm that $\text{T}_{2,1,0}$ effectively balances fine-grained precision with wide-range offset variations, maximizing available error-free columns.



