Again, we intend to make sure that $0.1\cdot v_{b_w}(g_{w})\leq (1-\sigma)v_{c_w}(g_{w})$, where $0.1$ is the intended lower bound for $\alpha_{b_w}$. We set the budget of $c_w$ to be $1000$. 



We then construct two goods $g_{(u,w)}$ for $b_u$ and $b_w$ and $g_{(v,w)}$ for $b_v$ and $b_w$ respectively. The values of these goods to the buyers are as follows.

\begin{equation*}
  v_{i}(g_{(u,w)})\coloneqq
