	\includegraphics[scale=0.75]{figures/horizon-set}
	\caption{\label{fig:horizon-sets} An illustration of how horizon sets help maintain weak consistency. With the same $u$, the reason for the different outcomes is that on the top, the small-tree split order \emph{restricted on} $V$ has changed compared to the last iteration. The use of the horizon set helps keep the small-tree split order \emph{invariant} before a root cut happens.}
