% \item Then, show that if the vertices in $T$ and $\Vp\setminus T$ are both consistent in $\cT_{\Vp\setminus T}$ and $\cT_{T}$, then, if $\lcatreeset{X}{\cTstar(\Vp)}$ only induces vertices in $\Vp\setminus T$ (resp. $T$), the consistent condition is already satisfied. 
