The paper \cite{Tol2023} presents a buildings heating model of dimension $4$, where the first state component is the indoor temperature and the other three are the temperatures in three layers of the wall separating the indoor space from the outdoor space. The matrix of the system of differential equations is
\begin{equation}
	A=\left[ 
	\begin{array}{rrrr}
		-5.7215   &    5.7215    &        0      &       0 \\
		0.23076   & -0.39276     &      0.162    &        0  \\
		0      &    0.081     &     -0.162    &    0.081 \\
