	$$
	in (\ref{epsilon<}). Therefore, the high non-normality affects the achievement of the asymptotic behavior for only $3.4629$ characteristic times.
\end{itemize}

Whereas the fact that the absolute condition number $\Vert \mathrm{e}^{tA}\Vert_2$ decays to zero in the long-time is not significant, the fact that the relative condition number $K(t,y_0)$  asymptotically becomes $K_\infty(y_0)$, and always remains of the same order of magnitude as $K_\infty(y_0)$, is highly significant.




