    \label{fig: tester Qtrue Vtrue}
\end{figure}
   \item[Case 2 ($v_1$ {\tt true,} $\neg v_1$ chosen):] Suppose the variable was assigned {\tt true} at the \emph{quantifier} stage and the $\exists$-player chooses the literal $\neg v_1$ at the \emph{literal chooser} stage.
   Figure \ref{fig: tester Qtrue Vfalse} shows a close-up of the upper (``false'') region from Figure~\protect\ref{fig: E-quantifier}, before the white Grasshopper 2 enters, with the rest of the pieces locked down. When white Grasshopper 2 enters from the left and lands on the indicated space, this does not free any piece. In fact, Black's pieces are in total lockdown, so White can win on the next turn by having white Grasshopper 2 jump northwest and surround the black Queen, or punish black for moving one of the dead pieces. Thus the $\forall$-player has a winning strategy, as desired.
