\begin{corollary}\label{cor: later E-quantifiers}
    If a literal $l \in \{v_i, \neg v_i \mid i \in \{1,3,5,\dots,n\}\}$ 
 is chosen during the \emph{literal chooser} stage, the $\exists$-player (Black) has a winning strategy if and only if $l$ is true under the variable assignment chosen during the \emph{quantifier} stage.
\end{corollary}



