\label{lem: A-quantifiers}
    If a literal $l \in \{v_i, \neg v_i \mid i \in \{2,4,6,\dots,n\}\}$ 
 is chosen during the \emph{literal chooser} stage, the $\exists$-player (Black) has a winning strategy if and only if $l$ is true under the variable assignment chosen during the \emph{quantifier} stage.    
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Again we assume, for now, the truth of Claim~\ref{claim: tester grasshoppers}. We proceed by case analysis. 
\begin{itemize}
     \item[Case 1 ($v_i$ {\tt true,} $v_i$ chosen):]  Suppose the variable was assigned {\tt true} at the \emph{quantifier} stage and the $\exists$-player chooses the literal $v_i$ at the \emph{literal chooser} stage. 
