We present our MCTS-style \bab tree exploration algorithm for verification of neural networks. The idea is that, we use counterexample potentiality to guide the search towards the sub-problems that are more likely to find counterexamples, so compared to the naive \bab, our tree exploration is imbalanced and favors the branches that are more ``\emph{promising}''. 

