\subsection{Related Work}

We briefly summarize relevant related work here, focusing on the \DkS{} problem, differential privacy for graph problems, and private principal component analysis (PCA).
Due to space constraints, we present a short summary here, and a longer discussion in \autoref{sec:related-appendix}.
Two graph privacy models have been considered-- node and edge DP.
There has been a lot of work on DP algorithms for computing graph properties, such as the cost of minimum spanning trees, counts of triangles and other small subgraphs, and community detection (primarily for the edge DP model), e.g.,~\cite{nissim2007smooth, karwa2014private, hay2009accurate, gupta2012iterative, farhadi2022differentially, nguyen2021differentially, kasiviswanathan2013analyzing, blocki2013differentially, dhulipala2022differential}.
This includes different kinds of density based problems~\cite{farhadi2022differentially, nguyen2021differentially, dhulipala2022differential}, but there has been no work on \DkS{} with DP.
Another related topic is  differentially private PCA~\cite{chaudhuri2012near, hardt2013beyond,  hardt2014noisy, blum2005practical, dwork2014analyze,balcan2016improved}; different strategies have been considered, including input perturbation~\cite{blum2005practical,dwork2014analyze}, output perturbation using smooth sensitivity~\cite{gonem2018smooth}, the exponential mechanism~\cite{kapralov2013differentially, chaudhuri2012near}, and the private power method \cite{hardt2013beyond,hardt2014noisy,balcan2016improved}.


